# .templatesyncignore — files KHoist OWNS, which template-sync never overwrites.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore. The weekly template-sync workflow
# (devantler-tech/.github .github/workflows/template-sync.yaml, using
# AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync) opens a PR that brings changes from the
# application template (the repository .github/workflows/template-sync.yaml names)
# into KHoist. It only ever touches files that exist in the template, and it SKIPS
# anything matched here.
#
# Everything NOT listed here is TEMPLATE-OWNED and kept current by template-sync —
# change it upstream in the application template, never by editing it here. KHoist
# receives .github/workflows/{template-sync,stale-issues,codeql}.yaml,
# .coderabbit.yaml and zizmor.yml. It owns the rest of what the template ships: its
# CI, CD and release callers, its lint configuration and its agent-instruction shims.
#
# merge-template-ignore-entries is on, so each sync ADDS the template's entries this
# list lacks: a file the template later marks as application-owned stays KHoist's.
# To receive a file the template lists, add the line `!<entry>` here instead.

# --- Identity & docs (KHoist's own) ---
AGENTS.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
.github/CODEOWNERS
.claude/skills/maintain/SKILL.md
# The shims carry a first-line heading for this repository's Markdown lint, so
# KHoist owns them and the check that enforces their exact shape.
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
scripts/validate-agent-shims.test.sh

# --- CI, CD, release and dependency config KHoist has outgrown the template's for ---
# KHoist publishes a signed controller image through publish-app and a signed AGE
# image, with its own smoke checks, instead of the template's single publish job, and
# selects exact CI coverage per change instead of the template's fixed jobs. Its release
# caller scopes the contents and identity permissions to the job, which
# scripts/release.test.sh requires. A sync must not replace any of these (#556).
.github/workflows/ci.yaml
.github/workflows/cd.yaml
.github/workflows/release.yaml
.github/workflows/todos.yaml
.github/workflows/publish-chart.yaml
# The template's Dependabot file is .yml; KHoist's is .yaml.
.github/dependabot.yml
.github/dependabot.yaml
.releaserc
.goreleaser.yaml
.gitignore
# .golangci.yml is KHoist's on purpose: its depguard rule is a strict allowlist,
# which KHoist extends with its own dependencies.
.golangci.yml
cspell.json
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.goreleaser
.dockerignore
# Copilot is disabled for this repository; never restore its agent setup workflow.
.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml

# --- Lint configuration ---
# KHoist's .mega-linter.yml stands alone: it does not extend the template's shared base,
# and nothing calls the template's lint workflow here. Its yamllint config reproduces
# MegaLinter's bundled behaviour plus two repository rules, and its Markdown is written
# against MegaLinter's bundled markdownlint rules. Receiving the template's copies would
# change what lint enforces on every file; adopting the shared base is a change of its own.
.mega-linter.yml
.github/mega-linter.base.yml
.github/workflows/lint.yaml
.yamllint.yml
.markdownlint.json
.editorconfig

# --- The application's overlays on shared configuration ---
.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml

# --- Tenant plumbing that guards the template's own CI and CD ---
# The template's pin checks guard the template's ci.yaml and cd.yaml. KHoist owns both,
# its CI does not run these checks, and Dependabot alone keeps its dependencies current,
# without Renovate. Remove these lines and wire the checks into ci.yaml to adopt them.
renovate.json
